{"id":"02b395ed6f22c079","group":"58","path":"58/batch01/58-thm-steel.md","title":"Woodin–Steel Derived Model Theorem","display":"thm-steel — Woodin–Steel Derived Model Theorem","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-steel","aliases":["58-thm-steel"],"display":"thm-steel — Woodin–Steel Derived Model Theorem","depends_on":["[[58-df-zfc-inner-derived-model]]","[[../batch18/58-df-determinacy]]","[[../batch11/58-df-class]]","[[../batch18/58-df-zfc-model6-sentence-set]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-steel"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-steel</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-steel — Woodin–Steel Derived Model Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"74261e48e94a4d06\" href=\"?note=74261e48e94a4d06\" title=\"58-df-zfc-inner-derived-model\">58-df-zfc-inner-derived-model</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"4cc4baec9297fd1e\" href=\"?note=4cc4baec9297fd1e\" title=\"../batch18/58-df-determinacy\">../batch18/58-df-determinacy</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"ca2a9c9166fa8cce\" href=\"?note=ca2a9c9166fa8cce\" title=\"../batch11/58-df-class\">../batch11/58-df-class</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"b00c32fa4e76ff85\" href=\"?note=b00c32fa4e76ff85\" title=\"../batch18/58-df-zfc-model6-sentence-set\">../batch18/58-df-zfc-model6-sentence-set</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\delta,\\mathbb P,G,\\mathbb R^*,\\Gamma^*\">\\(\\delta,\\mathbb P,G,\\mathbb R^*,\\Gamma^*\\)</span> (derived-model data) and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal D_\\delta\">\\(\\mathcal D_\\delta\\)</span> (the derived inner-model class)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcInnerDerivedModel}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcInnerDerivedModel}_S\\)</span> (derived-model class schema, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"74261e48e94a4d06\" href=\"?note=74261e48e94a4d06\" title=\"58-df-zfc-inner-derived-model\">58-df-zfc-inner-derived-model</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\theta_{\\mathrm{AD}^+}\">\\(\\theta_{\\mathrm{AD}^+}\\)</span> (a fixed sentence code for <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{AD}^+\">\\(\\mathrm{AD}^+\\)</span>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L_{\\in}\">\\(L_{\\in}\\)</span> (the membership language)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Class}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Class}_S\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcModel6SentenceSet}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcModel6SentenceSet}_S\\)</span> (class-code and sentence-set predicates from the dependencies)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ClassSatisfaction}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ClassSatisfaction}_S\\)</span> (external satisfaction predicate for membership structures with a proper-class carrier, defined below)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}class\\text{-}satisfaction}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n\\mathrm{ClassSatisfaction}_S(C,T)\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{Class}_S(C)\n\\land\\mathrm{ZfcModel6SentenceSet}_S(L_{\\in},T)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall\\varphi\\in T\\;\n\\langle C,\\in\\cap(C\\times C)\\rangle\n\\models_{\\mathsf{class}}\\varphi.\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}class\\text{-}satisfaction}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n\\mathrm{ClassSatisfaction}_S(C,T)\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{Class}_S(C)\n\\land\\mathrm{ZfcModel6SentenceSet}_S(L_{\\in},T)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall\\varphi\\in T\\;\n\\langle C,\\in\\cap(C\\times C)\\rangle\n\\models_{\\mathsf{class}}\\varphi.\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}steel}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n\\mathrm{ZfcInnerDerivedModel}_S\n(\\mathcal D_\\delta,\\delta,\\mathbb P,G,\\mathbb R^*,\\Gamma^*)\\\\\n&amp;\\to\\mathrm{ClassSatisfaction}_S\n(\\mathcal D_\\delta,\\operatorname{ZF}\\cup\\{\\theta_{\\mathrm{AD}^+}\\}).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}steel}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n\\mathrm{ZfcInnerDerivedModel}_S\n(\\mathcal D_\\delta,\\delta,\\mathbb P,G,\\mathbb R^*,\\Gamma^*)\\\\\n&amp;\\to\\mathrm{ClassSatisfaction}_S\n(\\mathcal D_\\delta,\\operatorname{ZF}\\cup\\{\\theta_{\\mathrm{AD}^+}\\}).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The conclusion now uses an explicit satisfaction relation for a proper-class membership structure. The set-coded four-place satisfaction predicate cannot be applied to <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal D_\\delta\">\\(\\mathcal D_\\delta\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>The premise imports the collapse, external genericity, derived reals, universally Baire pointclass, relativized constructibility, and the hypothesis that <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\delta\">\\(\\delta\\)</span> is a limit of Woodin cardinals.</li>\n<li>The theorem is metatheoretic because both the generic extension and the derived model are external class constructions.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"